.TH CROSS-DASHBOARD-CLI 1 "August 2026" "Cross-Dashboard 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cross-dashboard-cli \- command-line access to Cross-Dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cross-dashboard-cli task
.RI [ smart-text ]
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli capture
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli list
.I type
.RI [ --all ]
.RI [ --json ]
.RI [ --fuzzel ]
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli sync
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli waybar
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli pomo
.I type target
.RI [ --minutes N ]
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli pomo fuzzel
.RI [ --minutes N ]
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli pomo
.BR status | pause | resume | stop | toggle
.br
.B cross-dashboard-cli pomo task -u
.I uid
.RI [ --minutes N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses the same credentials, preferences, and SQLite cache as the native Linux GTK application.
Input for
.B task
and
.B capture
is read from standard input when no text arguments are supplied.
.PP
The
.B sync
command asks the persistent Cross-Dashboard systemd user service to refresh all configured
backends and waits for its completion signal. It does not perform a second in-process sync.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B task
Create a CalDAV task with the app's smart priority, tag, and natural-date parsing.
.TP
.B capture
Create a private memo on the configured Memos server.
.TP
.B list
List cached tasks, events, issues, notes, or Capture memos. Tasks default to active, events to
upcoming, issues to open, and memos to normal. Use
.B --all
to include inactive records.
Use
.B --fuzzel
for two tab-separated columns: a stable entity ID followed by friendly display text. This is
compatible with
.BR "fuzzel --dmenu --with-nth=2" .
.TP
.B sync
Request an immediate service-owned sync over the user D-Bus.
.TP
.B waybar
Continuously emit one JSON object per line for a Waybar custom module. It displays the shared
Pomodoro first, then a current event, overdue task, or nearest upcoming item.
.TP
.B pomo
Run a foreground terminal Pomodoro for a cached task, event, or issue. Title lookup ranks exact,
substring, and fuzzy matches, then asks for confirmation from a contextual list. Task choices show
their calendar, status, due date, and UID, so same-named and recurring tasks can be distinguished.
Use
.B -u UID
for exact task selection without an interactive chooser. Desktop notifications are shown at start
and completion; completed task sessions are appended to the task description.
Use
.B pomo fuzzel
to select across active tasks, upcoming events, and open issues. The service permits one global
timer at a time. Inspect or control it with
.BR "pomo status" ,
.BR "pomo pause" ,
.BR "pomo resume" ,
or
.BR "pomo stop" .
For status-bar integrations,
.B pomo toggle
opens Fuzzel while idle and pauses or resumes the active timer otherwise.
.SH SERVICE
Enable background sync and reminders with:
.PP
.EX
systemctl --user daemon-reload
systemctl --user enable --now crossdashboard.service
.EE
.PP
Inspect logs with:
.PP
.EX
journalctl --user -u crossdashboard.service
.EE
.SH BACKGROUND SNAPSHOTS
Inbox and Views can snapshot their current filters as a desktop background. The systemd user
service renders the PNG and invokes the command template configured in Settings. The template must
contain
.B %f
for the generated path. It is executed directly without a shell; pipelines, redirections,
substitutions, and daemonizing commands are unsupported. This integration is not available in the
Flatpak build.
